# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need, then reference it from
# docker-compose.yml (already wired up via `env_file: .env`).
#
# You don't need every variable below - only the ones for the CLI/provider
# combination you actually run (see README.md for the full breakdown).

# --- Claude Code (`claude` / `happy claude`) --------------------------------
# Required to run `claude` directly, or `happy claude`.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Codex CLI (`codex` / `happy codex`) ------------------------------------
# Required, UNLESS you set CODEX_BASE_URL below (BYOK).
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Codex BYOK: point Codex at your own OpenAI-Responses-API-compatible
# endpoint instead of api.openai.com. Independent of OPENAI_API_KEY above -
# set this instead if you're not using OpenAI's own API.
#
# CODEX_API_KEY is optional (a local/trusted gateway needs no key at all,
# and omitting it sends no auth header). CODEX_MODEL is optional too - sets
# the default model Codex uses.
#
# Note: Codex CLI only speaks the newer Responses API (/v1/responses), not
# the more common Chat Completions format most third-party
# "OpenAI-compatible" gateways implement - your endpoint has to actually
# support it, or requests will fail even though Codex starts fine.
# CODEX_BASE_URL=
# CODEX_API_KEY=
# CODEX_MODEL=

# --- Happy pairing (`happy claude` / `happy codex`) -------------------------
# No env var is required to START - if there's no valid Happy credential
# yet, the entrypoint runs Happy's pairing step on its own (QR code / link),
# BEFORE Claude Code or Codex start, then prints a HAPPY_CREDENTIALS_B64
# line and exits. Copy that line here and re-run the same command - it will
# skip pairing and go straight into your session. See README.md for the
# full walkthrough.
# HAPPY_CREDENTIALS_B64=
#
# Only set these if you're self-hosting Happy's own server instead of the
# hosted api.cluster-fluster.com one:
# HAPPY_SERVER_URL=
# HAPPY_WEBAPP_URL=
# HAPPY_HOME_DIR=
